  "decisions": {
    "k-perpetual": {
      "decision": "created",
      "reason": "Created n-perpetual-futures. Five coins whose metadata names perpetual-futures trading on four covered launchpads and three chains: Paper (Papertrade tagline) on Base and Robinhood Chain (Clanker; $51.3M and $10.7M), EmpireX (Pons, $0.84M), Purps (Meteora DBC, $0.39M) and Aloooong (pump.fun, $2.78M) - $66.0M combined 24h volume against the $500K bar, each with a market cap above $100K and no quarantine flag. Independent sources: Papertrade's own page and posts (e3:0, e3:1), @HyperEmpireX's 2026-10-16 launch post (e2:4) and 2026-10-17 trader posts about perp-backed memes (e3:2). Cautions recorded in the copy: the Paper pools are 20 and 4 hours old and no source links the contracts to Papertrade, the Base Paper trades about ten times its market cap, and Aloooong is a meme rather than a venue. Replaces n-programmable-rules at the cap (0.80M vs 66.0M 24h).",
      "narrativeId": "n-perpetual-futures"
    },
    "k-onchain": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "The word \"onchain\" over Paper x2 (placed in n-perpetual-futures), MUT8 (a brand coin: \"an onchain badge of loyalty\") and MADE (a founder-persona AI coin): only the Paper coins share a mechanism and they are already in the new narrative."
    },
    "k-exchange": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "The word \"exchange\" over Paper x2 (in n-perpetual-futures) and AVA (Holoworld AI utility token): no shared mechanism beyond the Paper coins."
    },
    "k-fully": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "The word \"fully\" over Paper x2 (in n-perpetual-futures) and MAKERS (market-making launchpad, pool 3 hours old): no shared mechanism beyond the Paper coins."
    },
    "k-elon": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "ELON (StonkFun), ELON (Meteora DBC) and GORK: the name only. Metadata is empty; the 2026-10-13 to 2026-10-17 posts (e2:1) are promotion for ELON Orbit, an \"Elon 2028\" coin and listing pushes, with no news or official source naming a shared story. Pools are 1 and 12 hours old."
    },
    "k-stocks": {
      "decision": "created",
      "reason": "Created n-stock-paired-coins. Four coins that tie memecoins to tokenized stocks on StonkFun, LaunchLab and pump.fun: STONK ($2.16M, \"Backed by stocks\"), OTC ($1.10M, \"earn stocks, pre-ipo, and yield\"), XSTOK ($0.40M, \"tokens paired with stocks\") and GTA6 ($0.31M, \"Earn $TTWO Stock\") - $3.98M combined 24h volume against the $500K bar, each above the $100K market cap bar with no quarantine flag. Independent sources: @xstokfun's 2026-10-16 launch posts (e3:3), @LaunchOnSF's $MUSK4 pairing post (e3:4), @otc_labs revenue posts (e2:3) and a 2026-10-15 trader post counting $31M of tokenized-stock rewards (e3:4). This resolves the lead deferred on 2026-10-15 and 2026-10-16 (two coins and BUBBLE): xstok opened on 2026-10-16 and is the third coin; GTA6 the fourth. BUBBLE (\"the Official coin for all ai stocks\") stays out: an AI-stocks meme with no pairing or reward mechanism. Replaces n-credits-for-holders at the cap (1.10M vs 3.98M 24h).",
      "narrativeId": "n-stock-paired-coins"
    },
    "k-earn": {
      "decision": "assigned",
      "reason": "OTC and GTA6 (both promise stock rewards) joined n-stock-paired-coins; MADE, MNRA (GPU compute coin) and BORRO (Robinhood Chain stock-token lending) share only the word \"earn\" and stay out.",
      "narrativeId": "n-stock-paired-coins"
    },
    "k-powered": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "The word \"powered\" over EMPIREX (in n-perpetual-futures), MIDWAY (privacy RWA layer) and AVA: no shared mechanism beyond EMPIREX's perpetuals story."
    },
    "k-fees": {
      "decision": "assigned",
      "reason": "WORLD (\"Fees to @iammarcmalone via UsePaid\", $1.19M) rejoined n-creator-fee-routing; MADE and MAKERS share only the word \"fees\" (MAKERS is a 3-hour-old market-making launchpad).",
      "narrativeId": "n-creator-fee-routing"
    },
    "k-roadster": {
      "decision": "assigned",
      "reason": "Two new Roadster coins joined n-flying-tesla-roadster: FTR \"Farting Tesla Roadster\" on pump.fun ($1.20M) and Flying Tesla Roadster on Flap ($0.24M). The StonkFun FTR (pool from August) predates the story and the Flap \"Roadster\" (market cap $70K) is under the $100K bar.",
